        "alternate_names": [
          "Australia's Cyber Security Strategy 2020",
          "Australia's Cyber Security Strategy 2016",
          "Australian Government Cyber Security Strategy 2009"
        ],
        "description": "Australia's flagship national cyber security strategy structured around six 'cyber shields' (Strong businesses and citizens; Safe technology; World-class threat sharing and blocking; Protected critical infrastructure; Sovereign capabilities; Resilient region and global leadership) and executed across three Horizons (Horizon 1: 2023–2025, Horizon 2: 2026–2028, Horizon 3: 2029–2030).",
        "notes": "Published November 22, 2023 alongside the Horizon 1 Action Plan (2023–2025), superseding the 2020, 2016, and 2009 strategies. Legislative pillars enacted via the Cyber Security Act 2024 (secid:regulation/homeaffairs.gov.au/cyber-security-act-2024).",
        "urls": [
          {
            "type": "website",
